A1. The longest distance between two points. (plur.) ~ DETOURS
A7. This blow-hard carried the house by storm. ~ CYCLONE
A13. The way the doctor looks when he is performing an operation. ~ INWARD
A14. Comparatively speaking this is the way Ghandi must feel. ~ COOLER
A15. What a good mixer always does. ~ STIRS
A16. Before Betty Coed was popular everyone tried to dance with Grace in this evening affair. ~ MINUET
A17. This is just one of the good bywords that Lowell Thomas uses. (You will get it before long.) ~ SO
A18. A rattling good member of the Smith family. ~ TIN
A19. Here is where you are going to get excited. ~ AGOG
A21. It is always a good sign if this comes before the rent. ~ TO
A22. When a Senator weighs his words this is what he gets. ~ TON
A23. If the meters are on the square this is the space covered. ~ AR
A24. One born every minute. ~ ROACH
A26. A headlight. ~ HALO
A27. Strictly fresh. ~ NEW
A29. A five spot. ~ PEDRO
A30. This house is just filled with beautiful orientals. ~ HAREM
A31. A beautiful clothes line. ~ ARRAY
A33. If it is possible to get a stout woman on this she will be sure to fall off. ~ DIET
A35. A self starter. ~ MY
A36. What Reno does every hour. ~ FREES
A37. A Georgian. ~ MACON
A39. A brief reply. ~ NO
